      "section": "RECALL",
      "title": "GOVERNING EQUATION: THE MESH",
      "body": "- Knudsen number is the mean free path divided by the length L\n- The mean free path is one over square root two, pi, d squared and n\n- The cell width must stay below the mean free path of the gas\n- That is why the reference grid is finer than the local spacing",
      "target_position": "the slide right after the step it governs, inside the same subsection.",
