      "section": "RECALL",
      "title": "GOVERNING EQUATION: THE GENETIC ALGORITHM",
      "body": "- A population of 50 designs runs for at most 200 generations\n- Tournament: three designs drawn at random, the cheapest one wins\n- So k_t sets the selection pressure: 3 is mild, a larger k is harsher\n- Crossover is applied with 0.7, mutation with 0.1 on every gene\n- It stops when the best cost stops improving by 1e-6 over 20 generations",
