    {
      "id": "recall-previous-issue-1",
      "section": "RECALL",
      "title": "PREVIOUS ISSUE 1: THE BAYESIAN STEP WAS WRONG",
      "body": "- The earlier assumption: the search was driven by an analytic model and a Bayesian expectation, so a surrogate of the model decided which candidate was worth simulating next.\n- The consequence: the acquisition step answered the question of the surrogate instead of the question of the design, and the surrogate had to be denoised before it could be used at all.\n- The evidence: the thesis removed the Bayesian-optimisation material and states that there is no central composite screen, no response surface, no surrogate and no acquisition step in the path.\n- The correction: the Latin hypercube seeds the genetic algorithm, every individual is scored with the closed-form cost, and the only high-fidelity runs are the validations of the pass-1 and the pass-2 winner.",
      "target_position": "the slide right after the elaboration of the second issue, closing the block of the previous issues.",
      "cards_only": true,
      "note": "What the third issue was. The earlier search was driven by an analytic model and a Bayesian expectation over a surrogate; the thesis removed that material and the double pass genetic algorithm took its place.",
      "footer": "The issue as it stood in the earlier work. The narration stays editable in PowerPoint.",
      "subsection": "Issues: Issue 1"
    },
    {
      "id": "recall-previous-issue-2",
      "section": "RECALL",
      "title": "PREVIOUS ISSUE 2: THE NARRATION WAS MISSING",
      "body": "- The earlier assumption: the standard CFD procedures and the supervisor's house style were carried into the slides as they stood, so every frame was a text frame and the words to say were never written down.\n- The consequence: the earlier decks hold no narration to carry over, so none of the spoken report could be ported into this one.\n- The evidence: the Week 14 deck carries 63 words in total, no speaker notes, and its content is two embedded videos with nine rasters, so there is no text there to port.\n- The correction: this first generation of presentation slides is authored from the verified state of the repository, one narration card per point, the owner blocks as the sections, and the thesis figures imported with their provenance.",
      "target_position": "the slide right after the elaboration of the third issue, closing the block of the previous issues.",
      "cards_only": true,
      "note": "What the fourth issue was. The narration of this report is the first one that was written, and this slide is the first generation of presentation slides that carries it.",
      "footer": "The issue as it stood in the earlier work. The narration stays editable in PowerPoint.",
      "subsection": "Issues: Issue 2"
    },
