      "title": "THESIS CONCLUSIONS: WHAT WAS FOUND",
      "body": "- Validation: Fay-Riddell 13.83 against 14.36 W/cm2, minus 3.7 percent; Sutton-Graves 15.36, plus 6.9 percent\n- Scalloping: peak flux 15.2 percent above the smooth body, element average 4.0 percent above\n- Regime: the Knudsen field spans transitional to near-continuum at 51.8 km, so DSMC is the right tool\n- Grid: drag converged by the third level, peak flux did not, so 139x139 stays the conservative choice\n- Optimisation: cost down 9.19 percent, drag coefficient up 2.14 percent, screening heat load up 5.96 percent",
